adjudication.rationale:
In store.js.es6, within the new plural-IDs hydration branch:

```js
const hydrated = obj[k].map(...);
obj[self.pluralize(subType)] = hydrated || [];
```

If `obj[k]` is an array, `Array.prototype.map` always returns an array object (truthy), so `hydrated || []` is indeed redundant. However, this is not a functional defect introduced by the diff—it's just unnecessary code. Also, if `obj[k]` were `null/undefined`, the code would throw before reaching `|| []`, so the fallback does not prevent an error. Therefore the finding is essentially a style/nit claim, not a real verifiable problem affecting correctness or behavior.
